Enable `allocator_api` on the suite's pinned nightly

Upstream now implements std::alloc::Allocator for its custom-mem allocators and uses
Box/Vec *_in unconditionally (MSRV 1.100; merged PR #560 "Custom allocators for real:
first steps", 2026-11-23). The suite builds with nightly-2026-08-24
(build-rust-harness.py), which predates the stabilization (nightly-2026-11-01 accepts
the same code), so the feature gate is needed there. Drop this patch once the suite
toolchain is bumped past the stabilization.
Upstream: none open (toolchain-only; gh search allocator/allocator_api, 2026-11-24).

diff --git a/c2rust-lib.rs b/c2rust-lib.rs
index b2abf2a..20b2662 100644
--- a/c2rust-lib.rs
+++ b/c2rust-lib.rs
@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@
 #![cfg_attr(all(feature = "nightly", test), feature(test))]
